Discover services with spans, logs or Metric datapoints in a running viewer. Group by exact typed service.namespace and service.name values, ordered by namespace then name and typed identity. Show distinct trace, span/error-span, log/error-log and Metric/datapoint/exemplar counts, plus lastSeen in Unix nanoseconds. JSON includes log severity bands; errorLogCount includes Error and Fatal. Exemplars belong to datapoints in the selected window. Counts describe stored telemetry, not requests or service health. Defaults to the last hour and 25 services. --service matches an exact name across namespaces. Pass serviceIdentity to services connections for incoming and outgoing connections. --json includes window bounds and truncation.

USAGE
  otel-desktop-viewer services [flags]

COMMANDS
  connections  Show incoming and outgoing service connections

EXAMPLES
  otel-desktop-viewer services
  otel-desktop-viewer services --service checkout --since 30m
  otel-desktop-viewer services --start 2026-10-02T08:00:00Z --end 2026-10-02T09:00:00Z --json

FLAGS
      --end string        Inclusive RFC3339 end time (nanoseconds supported)
      --endpoint string   Running viewer HTTP endpoint (default "http://localhost:8000")
      --json              Emit JSON with window bounds and truncation instead of columns
      --limit int         Maximum services to return (default 25)
      --service string    Only services with this exact name, across namespaces
      --since duration    Relative lookback window (for example 30m, 6h, or 24h) (default 1h0m0s)
      --start string      Inclusive RFC3339 start time (nanoseconds supported)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  -h, --help   Help for this command
